{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/160148-what-is-the-most-funded-pen-and-paper-rpg-of-all-time","id":160148,"title":"what is the most funded pen and paper rpg of all time?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-05T12:38:21-07:00","id":160148,"title":"what is the most funded pen and paper rpg of all time?","content":"as in using kickstarter, someone told me it was exalted 3 with mage coming close second.<br /> <br /> What about video games funded using kickstarter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T13:16:59-07:00","id":160180,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/inxile/torment-tides-of-numenera?ref=discovery\" target=\"_blank\">Torment: Tides of Numenera</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T13:33:07-07:00","id":160213,"title":"","content":"The <b>Ouya</b> game console clocked in with eight and a half million dollars, second highest funded Kickstarter of all time. If you want specifically games rather than a game console, <b>Torment: Tides of Numenera,</b> a single-player RPG attempting to be a spiritual sequel to the seminal classic, Planescape: Torment, and developed by several of the same people (including Planescape: Torment's lead writer), scored a little over four million dollars; there are two more video games <b>(Project Eternity</b> and <b>Mighty No. 9)</b> close behind in the high three million range.<br /> <br /> Traditional gaming Kickstarters trail behind. If you count miniatures sets, Reaper Miniatures raised three and a half million for an expansion to their <b>Bones miniatures line,</b> and then another three million for <b>a successor expansion.</b> Barring that, if you allow for tactical battlemap wargames, <b>Robotech RPG Tactics</b> raised one and a half million.<br /> <br /> Disallow miniatures sets, board games and wargames, and <b>Exalted Third Edition</b> does indeed top the list, but it hardly manages to punch at the video game weight class, having raised a still impressive six hundred thousand dollars, and nearly breaking seven hundred thousand. <b>Mage 20th Anniversary Edition</b> is in fact close behind, falling about ten thousand dollars short of the Exalted final tally. The closest pen &amp; paper contender to Mage is <b>Call of Cthulhu 7th Edition,</b> with five hundred sixty thousand dollars.<br /> <br /> Just for fun, here are some other projects that received more funding than any pen &amp; paper RPG on Kickstarter:<br /> <br /> <b>A pair of jeans</b> (seven hundred thousand dollars)<br /> <b>A web cartoon about sarcastic stick figures</b> (almost eight hundred thousand dollars)<br /> <b>A personal airborne surveillance drone</b> (nine hundred thousand dollars)<br /> <b>A hoodie</b> (one million dollars)<br /> <b>A device that attaches to paper airplanes to let you steer them with your smartphone</b> (one million dollars)<br /> <b>A WiFi enabled light bulb</b> (one million dollars)<br /> <b>A portable spectrometer with analysis app</b> (two million dollars)<br /> <b>A web show and in-school distribution for Reading Rainbow to teach kids to read</b> (three and a half million dollars and climbing \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/readingrainbow/bring-reading-rainbow-back-for-every-child-everywh?ref=discovery\" target=\"_blank\">you have almost a month left to donate!</a>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T14:04:50-07:00","id":160235,"title":"","content":"For non pen and paper games but tabletop board games kingdom death made something like 2.2m","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T15:12:23-07:00","id":160304,"title":"","content":"thanks for the info, you have satisfied my curiosity <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"ke